1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:18,410
A Place of Our Own

2
00:00:18,410 --> 00:00:22,160
I remember your parents' first house very well.

3
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:25,090
It was on Spring Avenue, near the park.

4
00:00:25,090 --> 00:00:26,530
I grew up in that house.

5
00:00:26,530 --> 00:00:28,780
Yes, and you were such a cute baby.

6
00:00:28,780 --> 00:00:30,800
I've seen pictures of him.

7
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:32,870
He had blond hair.

8
00:00:32,870 --> 00:00:34,380
I've been friendly with the Stewart family

9
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:35,090
for a long time,

10
00:00:35,090 --> 00:00:36,220
so it's my pleasure

11
00:00:36,220 --> 00:00:37,580
to help you find a house now.

12
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:39,850
Well, we're not sure we can afford one.

13
00:00:39,850 --> 00:00:41,150
But we'd like to find out

14
00:00:41,150 --> 00:00:42,140
about the possibilities.

15
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:44,150
That's a good idea.

16
00:00:44,150 --> 00:00:47,090
I love your house on Linden Street.

17
00:00:47,090 --> 00:00:50,050
I sold your father that house seventeen years ago.

18
00:00:50,050 --> 00:00:50,610
Really?

19
00:00:50,610 --> 00:00:52,680
Yes, Mom was pregnant with Robbie then,

20
00:00:52,680 --> 00:00:54,270
and they needed the extra room.

21
00:00:54,270 --> 00:00:56,650
I hear you're expecting a baby, Mrs. Stewart.

22
00:00:56,650 --> 00:00:57,250
Mmm-hmm.

23
00:00:57,250 --> 00:00:59,520
So we will be needing more room.

24
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:01,110
Oh, so you don't need something immediately?

25
00:01:01,110 --> 00:01:03,630
No. But in five or six months ...

26
00:01:03,630 --> 00:01:05,640
And time passes so quickly.

27
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:07,620
Yes, it does.

28
00:01:07,620 --> 00:01:08,530
Well, when you called,

29
00:01:08,530 --> 00:01:09,960
you gave me enough information

30
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:11,940
about your salaries and your savings.

31
00:01:11,940 --> 00:01:15,000
So I have a good idea about your financial situation.

32
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,280
Let me show you some pictures of houses.

33
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:19,120
With two bedrooms?

34
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:21,120
Yes, I think I can show you some.

35
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:23,220
Of course, they won't be in Riverdale.

36
00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:26,830
The cost of housing's too high for you here.

37
00:01:26,830 --> 00:01:29,800
I haven't thought about living anywhere else.

38
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:32,070
We've always lived in this area.

39
00:01:32,070 --> 00:01:34,410
Where should we look for a house, Mrs. Martinelli?

40
00:01:34,410 --> 00:01:36,330
Well, we have an office in Mount Kisco.

41
00:01:36,330 --> 00:01:37,500
It's a lovely area,

42
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:39,930
and it's only about an hour's drive from here.

43
00:01:39,930 --> 00:01:40,790
Here.

44
00:01:40,790 --> 00:01:45,340
I have a book with photos of some homes in that area.

45
00:01:45,340 --> 00:01:51,140
Now, let's see. Here.

46
00:01:51,140 --> 00:01:55,790
This is a lovely two-bedroom house in your price range.

47
00:01:55,790 --> 00:01:58,950
It's pretty,

48
00:01:58,950 --> 00:02:00,990
but I prefer a two-story home.

49
00:02:00,990 --> 00:02:02,210
I do, too.

50
00:02:02,210 --> 00:02:03,930
I don't care for a ranch type.

51
00:02:03,930 --> 00:02:07,770
OK.

52
00:02:07,770 --> 00:02:10,270
Oh, this is a wonderful house.

53
00:02:10,270 --> 00:02:11,210
I know it well.

54
00:02:11,210 --> 00:02:12,890
I sold it to the present owners.

55
00:02:12,890 --> 00:02:14,610
It looks wonderful.

56
00:02:14,610 --> 00:02:16,730
This is a two-bedroom, two-bath house.

57
00:02:16,730 --> 00:02:18,320
It has a full basement,

58
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:20,650
and it is on a half-acre lot.

59
00:02:20,650 --> 00:02:23,560
You can probably afford this one.

60
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:24,450
I like this house.

61
00:02:24,450 --> 00:02:25,770
So do I.

62
00:02:25,770 --> 00:02:27,620
And the price is right.

63
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:28,630
Would you like to go see it?

64
00:02:28,630 --> 00:02:29,790
Yes. We're planning

65
00:02:29,790 --> 00:02:32,180
to talk to someone at the bank next week.

66
00:02:32,180 --> 00:02:34,590
Perhaps we could see the house this weekend.

67
00:02:34,590 --> 00:02:36,030
If someone doesn't buy it before then,

68
00:02:36,030 --> 00:02:40,340
But let's keep looking.

69
00:02:40,340 --> 00:02:42,360
Just to get an idea of some other possibilities.

70
00:02:42,360 --> 00:02:47,060
This is very helpful, Mrs. Martinelli.

71
00:02:47,060 --> 00:02:47,940
Here.

72
00:02:47,940 --> 00:02:51,420
This is a wonderful example of Spanish-style architecture.

73
00:02:51,420 --> 00:02:52,330
Oh,

74
00:02:52,330 --> 00:02:55,600
I love the roof tiles on a Spanish-style house.

75
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:58,710
It looks like the houses in Hollywood.

76
00:02:58,710 --> 00:02:59,970
It's interesting.

77
00:02:59,970 --> 00:03:12,760
A house like this in Riverdale costs double the price.

78
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:15,550
Oh my!

79
00:03:15,550 --> 00:03:18,570
Here's a real buy.

80
00:03:18,570 --> 00:03:19,370
It's a bargain.

81
00:03:19,370 --> 00:03:22,070
This house just came on the market.

82
00:03:22,070 --> 00:03:22,990
It's quite lovely.

83
00:03:22,990 --> 00:03:24,750
Is it a two-bedroom house?

84
00:03:24,750 --> 00:03:27,640
No. It has three bedrooms and three baths.

85
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:28,980
I know the house.

86
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:30,400
It has a brand new kitchen.

87
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:33,750
And a living room with a twelve-foot ceiling.

88
00:03:33,750 --> 00:03:35,840
And there's a two-car garage.

89
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:37,630
Then why don't we go look at this house, too?

90
00:03:37,630 --> 00:03:39,960
It's a good investment.

91
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:41,100
Thank you, Mrs. Martinelli.

92
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:42,210
Thanks so much.

93
00:03:42,210 --> 00:03:43,980
My pleasure.

94
00:03:43,980 --> 00:03:45,900
Give my best to your parents.

95
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:48,350
Your father's a wonderful doctor, Richard.

96
00:03:48,350 --> 00:03:50,800
He took care of my daughter

97
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:52,970
when she was a child.

98
00:03:52,970 --> 00:03:53,340
He's the best pediatrician in Westchester.

99
00:03:53,340 --> 00:03:54,180
Thanks, Mrs. Martinelli.

100
00:03:54,180 --> 00:03:55,380
I'll give them your regards.

101
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:57,910
We really appreciate your advice.

102
00:03:57,910 --> 00:03:59,740
I do think you should go see the houses

103
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:01,210
and talk to the bank.

104
00:04:01,210 --> 00:04:01,800
Here.

105
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:09,510
Let me give you some information sheets about the houses.

106
00:04:09,510 --> 00:04:12,190
They're both very good buys.

107
00:04:12,190 --> 00:04:14,600
Well, thanks so much for your help and your time,

108
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:16,110
Mrs. Martinelli.

109
00:04:16,110 --> 00:04:17,650
We've got a lot to talk about.

110
00:04:17,650 --> 00:04:20,650
Mmm-hmm. Thanks.
